    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nThis may already be possible but I haven't found a way to do it yet. \r\n\r\nI want to open a file in a vertical or horizontal split. The example config provided in the docs opens the _currently open_ file in a new vert/horiz split, but I want to open the file that is under my cursor.",
